STYLE: A grand hand-made toy theatre production built from printed card. Every piece is a flat cutout of thick card about 4 mm thick, cut by hand with a craft knife. The front of each piece is printed like an illustration from an old Indonesian school textbook of the 1980s: warm gouache and ink drawn by hand, soft rounded shapes, gentle friendly faces with simple dot eyes, clean ink outlines, printed on slightly yellowed paper with visible halftone dots and a little colour misregistration at the edges, like an old offset print. Flat colour with soft gouache shading, warm afternoon light. Bold, clear shapes that read from the back row. Puppet joints are brass split pins. Palette: old paper #EFE4C8, school white #F6F1E4, navy #2D3E66, school red #C7413A, flame red #D9452B, field ochre #D8A651, grass green #7A9A4A, sky blue #8FB4CF, ink #2B2620, with raw card brown #A57E52 at cut edges. The mood is warm, nostalgic and tender.
CONSTRAINTS: No text, no characters, no letters, no numbers, no writing on blackboards or books or signs, no logos, no flags, no signature, no watermark. No photographic people, no 3D render look, no plastic, no glossy finish, no anime style.
REFERENCES: Image 1 is the look reference. Match its old textbook gouache and ink, halftone print, palette, raw card edges and figure style. Do not copy its composition.
SUBJECT: The four pieces of a marionette of young Dimas, an Indonesian boy of fourteen, facing three-quarters to the left: (1) the head with messy short black hair, a bright cheeky face and the bare neck; (2) the body from the neck base down to black school shoes and white socks, a white short-sleeved school shirt untucked, navy blue shorts, and a small school bag strap, standing, with NO arms; (3) the right arm from a short white sleeve to an open hand holding a small blank white envelope; (4) the left arm from a short white sleeve to an open waving hand. The head is a boy's size for this body.
COMPOSITION: A flat lay of the separate cardboard pieces of ONE jointed puppet, all at the same scale, seen straight from the front on a transparent background. Each piece is a separate cutout with clear empty space around it. No piece touches or overlaps another piece. No shadow, no rod, no strings, no stand, no stage.
JOINTS: The body has three clearly visible round brass split pins: one at the centre of the base of the neck and one on each shoulder. The body ends at the neck base with no head and has no arms. The head piece ends in a bare neck with no collar, with one brass pin at the bottom of the neck. Each arm piece has one brass pin at the very top of the shoulder. The head is drawn at the same scale as the body, a normal adult size for the body.
